[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b2: where does the clustering turn on?
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   The two competing pictures predict different radial structure.
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   * Point-mass shepherding: confinement should strengthen with
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   semimajor axis (the perturber dominates the most distant
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   orbits) and cluster membership should track the perturber's
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   secular reach -- a smooth, monotonic trend.
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   * Fixed spatial boundary (TEP): orbits are phase-locked by the
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   proper-time field where they *are*, so clustering should
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   switch on at a fixed spatial radius.  The natural coordinate
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   is then the orbit's spatial extent -- aphelion distance ad =
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   a(1+e) -- not the semimajor axis itself.  A transition at
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   fixed ad independent of a is the "domain wall" signature.
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   Scans performed (all on the secure catalog, cc<=3):
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   W1  sliding windows in log a (0.4 dex, 0.1 dex step):
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   R(varpi), R(omega), R(Omega) and conditioned p(varpi)
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   per window -- element selectivity shows which part of the
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   anomaly turns on where.
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   W2  threshold scans: for each of a_min, ad_min, q_min, the
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   clustering of the tail sample x > x_min vs threshold --
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   locates the turn-on in each coordinate.
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   W3  change-point estimate: the radius x* that best splits the
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   population into unclustered (inside) and clustered
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   (outside) subsamples, in each of a, ad, q -- the wall
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   radius.  A sharp, coordinate-consistent transition
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   supports the boundary picture; a smeared or
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   coordinate-dependent one supports shepherding.
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   Statistics: conditioned null as in step 02 (fix a,e,i; om,w
[2026-09-20 10:42:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 012]   uniform; 5000 MC per window for the scan, 20000 at key points).
